  "name": "fold-studio",
  "vibe": "An origami studio in washi #f2ede3, with Zilla Slab set in warm #26221c, one vermilion (#d64545) and one deep indigo (#2e4a7d). The world folds: three large translucent triangles squash and stretch on independent sine phases while slowly rotating, so sheets appear to crease open and shut; a small vermilion crane flies across the upper third with wing points that actually flap on a 4Hz beat; four dashed diagonals sit underneath like crease-pattern guides. Corners are near-square everywhere — chips are literal squares, tiles round at 4px, cards at 6 — and the camera carries a 2° skew, and it tips its own plane like a held sheet. Titles and items both flip in. Owns an assemble DragDrop, a flip Swipe, fade Morphs and switch Toggles. For workshops, classes, stationery, studios and patient handmade work.",
